  "summary": "Signed multilayer methods and structurally regularized dynamics now resolve network-level differences in HCP subjects and cocaine use disorder.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is graph-based characterization of brain organization at the network level. A signed multilayer community-detection framework produces mesoscale functional connectome fingerprints, evaluated on 810 HCP subjects across sessions. Separately, diffusion-prior Laplacian smoothing of dynamic connectivity reveals reduced functional flexibility in cocaine use disorder, with structural constraints built into the dynamics model. The published item is less directly network-based: gsModel uses spatial transcriptomics cell-type composition to classify macaque sulci versus gyri at over 90% accuracy. What is new across these is the explicit incorporation of sign, multilayer structure, and structural priors into functional network inference.",
